  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n\n1.1 Main construction\n\nThe exact available objective is a finite-support max-correlation problem. For a discrete candidate `h` of length `n`,\n\n`dx = 2.0 / n`  \n`target = n / 2.0`  \n`raw(h) = np.correlate(h, 1.0 - h, mode=\"full\")`  \n`C5 = dx * max(raw(h))`\n\nsubject to `0 <= h_i <= 1` and `sum_i h_i = n/2`. The evaluator is authoritative: the raw profile length is `2n-1`, it is not circular, and each lag endpoint uses exactly the correlation called by the evaluator.\n\nThe prior approach suggests that the search must pay close attention to multiple simultaneous active lag constraints. The proposed method is materially different because the principal global optimizing direction is not a smooth gradient vector or a one-coordinate move, but a convex linear program in all coordinates. For the current vector `h0`, select a set of high-value lags and build linearized overlap constraints using the current complement `1 - h0`. Then solve a trust-region LP over:\n\nminimize a scalar minimax level `t`  \nsubject to selected linearized overlap values `<= t`  \n`sum x = target`  \n`0 <= x_i <= 1`  \n`x_i` close to `h0_i`.\n\nAt the starting vector the linearized constraints match the actual raw values for each selected lag. The resulting full-vector LP proposal `x_lp` is examined by the true evaluator; if accepted, it is used both as a full candidate and as a zero-sum direction `d = x_lp - h0` for an exact one-dimensional finite-support line search. The line search can accept a granular improvement between `0` and the LP proposal. Other safe line directions use the same exact one-dimensional correction formulas. Every candidate that is returned must first be repaired to the exact feasible set and re-scored with the true objective.\n\nThe use of a whole-vector LP and local trust box is central and different: instead of constructing a few one-dimensional gradients around the current point, we solve an active-lag polyhedral relaxation in dimension `n+1`. The exact model protects this method from being misled by the nonconvex complement. The original product remains bilinear and nonconvex, so the method is not a global globalness proof. Exact acceptance-one stays object guarantee no retention. Allow recent surrog meta stability although maintain injured.\n\n1.2 Why this may improve near 0.380889\n\nThe target required improvement is very close to the parent bound. A near-optimal vector usually has several large active lag functions that cannot all be improved by random pair moves. The LP generates vertices inside the feasible-cap squeeze where selected affine upper extensions are as equal and as low as possible. The line search tests those vertices well in overlap alterations. Using envies the optimum, leantiatric SP direction. Accepted each exact unchanged due this defining rules no regret, own.\n\nPotential limitations supported: exact value produced at a Feas bounds. Means starting parent occup voucher. No global performance ending poor stagnation. Those mitigate preserving active que schedule best delic mass\u0633\u064a\u062c ctx retry, shorter linked embodiment lab local attach alternative.\n\nComplex schedule blocks proving limits speed bound Success.",
